-- title:
--   Base change of points of the Hilbert functor
-- statement:
--   Fix $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and a function $h : \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{N}$, and let $A \to B$ be a homomorphism of commutative rings, i.e. $B$ an $A$-algebra. Let $P$ be a point of the Hilbert functor over $A$, that is: an ideal $P.I$ of $A[x_0,\dots,x_n] =$ `MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) A` such that every homogeneous component of every element of $P.I$ again lies in $P.I$, and such that for each degree $d$ the $A$-module $\mathrm{piece}(P.I, d)$ — the $A$-submodule of degree-$d$ homogeneous polynomials modulo its intersection with $P.I$ — is a finite $A$-module, a projective $A$-module, and has $\mathrm{rankAtStalk}$ equal to $h(d)$ at every prime of $A$. The assertion is that there exists a point $Q$ of the Hilbert functor over $B$, for the same $n$ and the same function $h$, whose underlying ideal $Q.I$ is the ideal of $B[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ generated by the image of $P.I$ under coefficientwise application of $A \to B$, i.e. $Q.I = P.I.\mathrm{map}\,(\mathrm{MvPolynomial.map}\,(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,A\,B))$.
--
--   This is the functoriality clause for the Hilbert functor of $\mathbb{P}^n$: a point with Hilbert function $h$ over $A$ extends along any ring map $A \to B$ to a point with the same Hilbert function $h$. It is used in the Hilbert-functor representability argument and in the accompanying statements about membership of $X^k$-multiples in the ideals of points with a given Hilbert function.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_HilbertFunctor_exists_point_I_eq_map.lean

